summary:
  A parked station whose relay tap dies is read as a stall, and the stall
  timer's answer to a stall is to play again.

history:
  The third road to the same complaint on #13, and the quietest. The stall
  timer exists so a station that goes silent mid-song comes back without the
  listener noticing, and it backs off 15 s, 30 s, 1, 2, 4 minutes up to five.
  A relay tap dying under a park reaches the player as StalledMedia, which is
  indistinguishable from a real stall in there — so the timer restarted the
  source and called play(), once per backoff round, for as long as the session
  lasted. That is the "repeatedly" in the report. Found 2026-09-18 after the
  heal and preview roads were closed, by asking which OTHER timer can end in
  audio.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
              if (root._tsPaused) return;

replace:
              if (false) return;

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_every_automatic_recovery_road_asks_the_intent_not_the_state.
  Line-neutral.
